Follow the package through filling, delivery, use and return (@cs-packaging: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @chemical-supply-systems, #source "../sources/Chemical-Warehousing-HSE-HSG71.lingua#r_6MKP347GP6BY1H1PCKCJKAV91R", #source "../sources/Dangerous-Goods-Model-Regulations-UN.lingua#r_608ADXFZHPBDY8MYGJZ9M1BG06", #source "../sources/Cargo-Transport-Units-Code.lingua#r_4YS4SQPG6WKX5TWAF48M0VV9X1", #source "../sources/Pharmaceutical-Starting-Materials-WHO.lingua#r_7H51215T44S69TD3R0499VMTTY", #chemical-supply-systems "Tanks-working-capacity-heel-headspace-and-receiving-state.lingua#r_204ACMY61P8Y550HJ4WAESXZVS") { r_751D7AQJ8V8K3CGTJDPFX953R3
**Read:** [Chemical warehousing — HSE HSG71](../sources/Chemical-Warehousing-HSE-HSG71.lingua#r_6MKP347GP6BY1H1PCKCJKAV91R), complete packaged-storage and handling sections; [Recommendations on the Transport of Dangerous Goods — UN Model Regulations](../sources/Dangerous-Goods-Model-Regulations-UN.lingua#r_608ADXFZHPBDY8MYGJZ9M1BG06), the complete applicable packaging, marking and empty-package provisions; [Code of Practice for Packing of Cargo Transport Units — IMO, ILO and UNECE](../sources/Cargo-Transport-Units-Code.lingua#r_4YS4SQPG6WKX5TWAF48M0VV9X1), complete relevant packing, responsibilities and receiving sections; [Good trade and distribution practices for pharmaceutical starting materials — WHO](../sources/Pharmaceutical-Starting-Materials-WHO.lingua#r_7H51215T44S69TD3R0499VMTTY), the complete repackaging and documentation requirements.

Compare a bottle, drum, intermediate bulk container and bag for an actual chemical grade and use. Include contact material, closure, fill/empty state, identity, protection, handling and the evidence required for transport. Package choice affects contamination, sample representativeness, damage probability, unit load and work at the receiving site.

Draw a package's complete cycle. Separate manufacturer qualification, cleaning/inspection, filling, sealing/identification, dispatch, receipt, controlled issue and return or disposal. For reuse, specify how previous contents and changed package condition are known. An empty uncleaned package can retain consequential material even when its useful contents have been consumed.

Use the dangerous-goods and CTU material in its actual scope rather than assuming that a robust-looking container is suitable. Compare one-way and returnable arrangements on material recovery, cleaning resources, contamination evidence, travel and loss. State who maintains the package pool and how a failed inspection affects availability. Develop an explicit package-count and material-residual balance for one delivery cycle. Keep external certification/testing details linked to their primary documents and distinguish a classroom design proposal from a physically qualified packaging system.

**Continue:** [Distinguish nominal tank volume from usable receiving and supply capacity](Tanks-working-capacity-heel-headspace-and-receiving-state.lingua#r_204ACMY61P8Y550HJ4WAESXZVS).

